\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Midland-Odessa is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Midland-Odessa's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Midland-Odessa has set <strong>53 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 102 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">181 record highs</strong>, far more than the 102 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (74). Midland-Odessa's all-time high is 116\u00b0F, on June 27, 1994.","t_chg":"Midland-Odessa has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 95 complete years: Midland-Odessa's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.29\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +0.40), about +2.7\u00b0F since 1931. Midland-Odessa's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.23\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.35), about +2.1\u00b0F since 1931.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Midland-Odessa's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.24 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 13.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1986 (32.13 in); the driest, 1951 (4.60 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 16 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}